# Package boundaries (§14.1–14.2)

Dependencies only point **down**. A package never imports from its own layer (except the listed same-layer edges) or from a layer above it.

```
L6 apps/web
L5 ui · workers/*
L4 client
L3 sim · import
L2 domain · catalog · render · storage · rpc
L1 schema
L0 math
```

| Package | May depend on |
|---|---|
| math | nothing |
| schema | math |
| domain | math, schema |
| catalog | math, schema, inversify |
| render | math, schema, catalog, inversify. **Never domain**: client adapts domain data into render buffers. |
| storage, rpc | schema, inversify |
| sim | math, schema, domain |
| import | math, schema, domain, catalog, compile-wasm |
| client | domain, catalog, render, storage, rpc, inversify; **`import type` only** from sim and import |
| workers/* | rpc, their engine (sim / import / later render) and its deps, inversify |
| ui | client (interfaces, tokens, view models), `import type` from schema |
| apps/web | ui, client, inversify, workers (only as `new Worker(new URL(..., import.meta.url), { type: "module" })`) |
| tools/asset-pipeline | math, schema, domain, catalog, brick-compile CLI. Nothing imports it. |
| tools/oxlint-plugin | `@oxlint/plugins` only. Loaded by `.oxlintrc.json`, never imported by code. |

- **Pure packages** (`math`, `schema`, `domain`, `sim`) use no DOM, `window`, three.js, IndexedDB, `Worker`, `fetch` or Inversify. They must run unchanged in Node.
- Import other packages only through their `package.json` `exports` (`@brr/domain`), never `@brr/domain/src/...` or relative paths across packages.
- `packages/compile-wasm` is generated output. Change `crates/brick-compile-wasm` instead.
- Every new edge must be declared in `package.json` deps (`workspace:*`), in tsconfig `references` once project references are in use, and in the boundary config once one is added (Turborepo `boundaries` or dependency-cruiser). If an edge isn't in the table above, don't add it. Ask.
